# Byte-for-byte. No end-of-line conversion, in either direction.
#
# This project has already lost real time to line endings. publish.cmd had 839
# bare LFs and zero CRLFs, and cmd.exe mis-parsed it — executing fragments of
# REM and echo lines as commands, which is what produced "App version: unknown",
# a zip named for that unknown version, and a build that silently packaged a
# stale exe. It only works as CRLF.
#
# Meanwhile install.cmd and uninstall.cmd are LF, work correctly that way, and
# ship inside the release zip — so rewriting them would make the repo disagree
# with an artifact already published. INSTALL-README.txt carries a UTF-8 BOM for
# the same "matches what shipped" reason.
#
# Git's default on Windows would convert all of this on checkout. It must not.
* -text
